    "text": "<p>For the four circles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>O</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;following four equations are given:</p><p>Circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>If the centre of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is joined with centre of the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;further centre of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> is joined with centre of the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo></math> centre of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is joined with the centre of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and lastly, centre of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is joined with centre of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then these lines form the sides of a</p>",
